    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Looks cool! Is this open source infra or an api hosted by you?</p>",
        "id": 577610039,
        "sender_full_name": "Ralph Furman",
        "timestamp": 1772749705
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's a hosted API for now :)</p>",
        "id": 577610612,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1772749946
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Cool! I'm most excited about sorry2lemma, I'd love to have that in my vscode!</p>",
        "id": 577610996,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Flatt",
        "timestamp": 1772750123
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"956055\">Oliver Flatt</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/219941-Machine-Learning-for-Theorem-Proving/topic/Axiom.20Lean.20Engine/near/577610996\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Cool! I'm most excited about sorry2lemma, I'd love to have that in my vscode!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This seems to be calling <code>extract_goal</code> behind the scenes (or something very very similar), you can do that yourself in VSCode. (edit: the <a href=\"https://axle.axiommath.ai/v1/docs/tools/sorry2lemma/\">docs</a> agree)<br>\nBut like <code>extract_goal</code>, it is often broken because it uses output from the pretty-printer which can omit necessary details.</p>",
        "id": 577617273,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1772753306
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yup, exactly. As <code>extract_goal</code> suggests we do also include some <a href=\"https://axle.axiommath.ai/v1/docs/tools/have2lemma/#verbosity\">options</a> to include those necessary details, but it's not perfect</p>",
        "id": 577618427,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1772753907
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Very cool work! Will there be a technical report released in the future like that for Aristotle or SeedProver?</p>",
        "id": 577658279,
        "sender_full_name": "Siyuan Ge",
        "timestamp": 1772775726
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've created an open source version of something similar to (but more powerful than) <code>sorry2lemma</code> (and several other things described here) as part of <a href=\"https://github.com/KellyJDavis/goedels-poetry/\">goedels-poetry</a> to allow <a href=\"https://github.com/KellyJDavis/goedels-poetry/\">goedels-poetry</a> to recursively decompose and prove theorems.</p>\n<p>It takes a theorem with sorry proven have statements, e.g.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">erdos_1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSumDistinctSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lemma1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">....</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lemma2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">....</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lemma3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">....</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>then extracts standalone lemmas (e.g. lemma1, lemma2, lemma3...) such that each can be proven independently. Among other things, this adds the hypotheses of the enclosing theorem to the hypotheses of each lemma and adds texturally earlier lemmas as hypotheses to texturally later theorems (e.g. the standalone version of lemma2 will have lemma1 a hypothesis.)</p>\n<p>I've not, however, packaged this code for external consumption. The core code implementing it is <a href=\"https://github.com/KellyJDavis/goedels-poetry/blob/811cb623f9080e95c53efe246ce0bc4cae40e25b/goedels_poetry/agents/sketch_decomposition_agent.py#L308\">here</a>. It uses <a href=\"https://github.com/KellyJDavis/repl\">repl</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/KellyJDavis/ast_export\">ast_export</a> as exposed by <a href=\"https://github.com/KellyJDavis/kimina-lean-server\">kimina-lean-server</a> to do the heavy lifting.</p>",
        "id": 577661532,
        "sender_full_name": "Kelly Davis",
        "timestamp": 1772778028
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Made (well, asked Claude) an MCP server to make it easier to call these tools from Claude Code: <a href=\"https://github.com/Vilin97/axle-mcp\">https://github.com/Vilin97/axle-mcp</a></p>",
        "id": 577698871,
        "sender_full_name": "Vasily Ilin",
        "timestamp": 1772788785
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"763766\">Siyuan Ge</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/219941-Machine-Learning-for-Theorem-Proving/topic/Axiom.20Lean.20Engine/near/577658279\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Very cool work! Will there be a technical report released in the future like that for Aristotle or SeedProver?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Perhaps! For now it'll just be the web docs</p>",
        "id": 577812068,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1772821570
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"414458\">Vasily Ilin</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/219941-Machine-Learning-for-Theorem-Proving/topic/Axiom.20Lean.20Engine/near/577698871\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Made (well, asked Claude) an MCP server to make it easier to call these tools from Claude Code: <a href=\"https://github.com/Vilin97/axle-mcp\">https://github.com/Vilin97/axle-mcp</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Haha awesome -- for the record, we also mocked up an MCP server <a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/axiom-axle-mcp/\">here</a> if it proves useful. This one has the benefit of auto-updating when Axle itself updates. (not heavily tested though)</p>",
        "id": 577813656,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1772822194
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Forwarding a quick announcement : we forgot to update some settings for rate limits and so they were unintentionally too restrictive.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>API key users: increased to 20 active requests (up from 4)</li>\n<li>Anonymous users: increased to 10 active requests (up from 1)</li>\n<li>Max timeout: increased to 15 minutes (up from 5 minutes)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Users with an API key should regenerate their key to apply the new limits.</strong></p>",
        "id": 577859288,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1772842196
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are you aiming for feature parity with <a href=\"https://github.com/oOo0oOo/lean-lsp-mcp\">Lean-lsp-mcp</a>?<br>\nFor example, <code>lean_hover_info</code>, <code>lean_get_widgets</code>, <code>lean_local_search</code>, <code>lean_loogle</code>, <code>lean_leansearch</code> are particularly useful.</p>",
        "id": 577952788,
        "sender_full_name": "Vasily Ilin",
        "timestamp": 1772928339
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My <code>example01.lean</code> file:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test01</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It appears that AXLE was unable to disprove the theorem above.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Fish\"><pre><span></span><code>chabulhwi@desktop ~/l/l/P/Examples <span class=\"o\">(</span>master<span class=\"o\">)&gt;</span> axle disprove example01.lean --environment lean-4.27.0 --ignore-imports\nError: unknown free variable <span class=\"err\">`</span>_fvar.32<span class=\"err\">`</span>\n\nPlease check your input <span class=\"k\">and</span> try again.\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 578064991,
        "sender_full_name": "Bulhwi Cha",
        "timestamp": 1773025915
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>My counterexample</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test01</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- If `a` is a minimal element of a type `α` with respect to a binary relation `r`, then it is</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">accessible through `r`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">acc_of_is_min</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hxa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hxa</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ba</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc_lt_c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">acc_of_is_min</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc_lt_b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc_lt_c</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc_lt_a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc_lt_b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not_test01</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">},</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hca</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc_lt_a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ba</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cb</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hnca</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hnca</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hca</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 578065437,
        "sender_full_name": "Bulhwi Cha",
        "timestamp": 1773026323
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"414458\">Vasily Ilin</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/219941-Machine-Learning-for-Theorem-Proving/topic/Axiom.20Lean.20Engine/near/577952788\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Are you aiming for feature parity with <a href=\"https://github.com/oOo0oOo/lean-lsp-mcp\">Lean-lsp-mcp</a>?<br>\nFor example, <code>lean_hover_info</code>, <code>lean_get_widgets</code>, <code>lean_local_search</code>, <code>lean_loogle</code>, <code>lean_leansearch</code> are particularly useful.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thanks Vasily -- yea, we are looking into integrating this at some point. Atm Axle's features are just based on some specific internal needs</p>",
        "id": 578204495,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773074356
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"417769\">@Bulhwi Cha</span> Thanks for the example. Two things --</p>\n<ol>\n<li>That error is a bug, thanks for catching that! It will be fixed in the next deployment.</li>\n<li>Unfortunately, even with that bug fixed, <code>disprove</code> is not strong enough to find this counterexample :)</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 578226678,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773080326
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>is this tool just based on LeanVerify?</p>",
        "id": 578233982,
        "sender_full_name": "Leni Aniva",
        "timestamp": 1773082899
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry I'm not familiar with that, or do you mean SafeVerify?</p>",
        "id": 578239053,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773084911
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"951303\">Jimmy Xin</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/219941-Machine-Learning-for-Theorem-Proving/topic/Axiom.20Lean.20Engine/near/578239053\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sorry I'm not familiar with that, or do you mean SafeVerify?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>my bad. i meant SafeVerify</p>",
        "id": 578245643,
        "sender_full_name": "Leni Aniva",
        "timestamp": 1773087317
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>verify_proof drew heavily from SafeVerify but it doesn't quite have the same behavior; particularly, in some situations it's \"less safe\" than SafeVerify or comparator. That was a tradeoff we made for scalability gains which we discuss a bit in the docs :)</p>",
        "id": 578254365,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773090675
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"951303\">@Jimmy Xin</span> IIUC from the <a href=\"https://axle.axiommath.ai/v1/docs/tools/verify_proof/\">docs</a>, <code>verify_proof</code> doesn't handle environment hacks, like the standard</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"k\">#eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CoreM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Declaration.defnDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`oops</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">levelParams</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkConst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``False</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkConst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``True.intro</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">hints</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">regular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">safety</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">safe</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getEnv</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ok</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env.addDeclCore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">doCheck</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"error\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">setEnv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">oops</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 578263312,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Topaz",
        "timestamp": 1773094406
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you give some indication for what it <em>does</em> guard against?</p>",
        "id": 578263344,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Topaz",
        "timestamp": 1773094418
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"243562\">Adam Topaz</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/219941-Machine-Learning-for-Theorem-Proving/topic/Axiom.20Lean.20Engine/near/578263344\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can you give some indication for what it <em>does</em> guard against?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Ya. verify_proof is intended to prevent more benign \"mistakes\" such at those that listed <a href=\"https://axle.axiommath.ai/v1/docs/tools/verify_proof/#verification-error-messages\">here</a></p>",
        "id": 578264529,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773094922
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For our pipelines, we like using verify_proof when we need checks at scale, and then fallback to comparator or similar when we need a final, strong guarantee!</p>",
        "id": 578264940,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773095123
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay, so it never actually replays the environment?</p>",
        "id": 578265017,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Topaz",
        "timestamp": 1773095164
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nope</p>",
        "id": 578265060,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773095185
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the quick response! One more question: I heard claims that Axiom’s verifier is “100x faster” than comparator. Is this claim referring to <code>verify_proof</code>?</p>",
        "id": 578272449,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Topaz",
        "timestamp": 1773098746
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes. </p>\n<p>(Though I'm not the biggest fan of those claims, as they do tend to be dependent on the exact nature of the requests and the concurrency... )</p>",
        "id": 578275439,
        "sender_full_name": "Jimmy Xin",
        "timestamp": 1773100372
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Understood. Thank you for the clarifications!</p>",
        "id": 578275620,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Topaz",
        "timestamp": 1773100491
    },
